.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- create zip archives using colon-path member names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I zipfile
.I path
\&...
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
is a colon-path aware wrapper around
.BR zip (1).
By default (when
.B COLON_WRAP
is unset), a built-in rewrite implementation stores colon-path sources
under their
.I LEAF
names in the archive.
Set
.B COLON_WRAP=1
to invoke
.B zip
from
.B PATH
instead.
.PP
Sources given as
.B BASE:LEAF
are stored in the archive under
.I LEAF
(not under the full physical path
.BR BASE/LEAF ).
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.PP
The wrapper stages leaf names (via symlinks) and runs
.B zip \-r
from that staging directory unless
.B \-r
was already supplied.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B @COLON@ a.zip a/b:c/d/e
Creates
.B a.zip
whose members are rooted at
.B c/d/e/
(from physical tree
.BR a/b/c/d/e ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Show the planned
.B zip
invocation without executing it.
When using the built-in rewrite (default), output is prefixed with
.BR (rewrite) .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recurse\-paths
Recurse into directories.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Update only if archive member is newer.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delete
Delete entries in zipfile that are not on disk.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-move
Move files into zipfile (delete originals).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-junk\-paths
Store only the basename of each file.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-symlinks
Store symlinks as the link instead of the file.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude=GLOB
Exclude files matching
.IR GLOB .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-include=GLOB
Include only files matching
.IR GLOB .
.TP
.BR \-0\ .\.\-9
Compression level (0=store, 9=best).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-encrypt
Encrypt archive entries.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-password=PASS
Set password for encryption.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-fix
Try to repair a damaged archive.
.TP
.B \-FF
Try harder to repair a damaged archive.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-adjust\-suffix
Adjust self-extracting exe suffix.
.TP
.BR \-FS ", " \-\-filesync
Sync changed files only.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-no\-extra
Do not save extra file attributes.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-grow
Grow existing archive.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-latest\-time
Set zip entry time to newest file time.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-temp\-path=DIR
Use
.I DIR
for temporary files.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-suffix=SUFFIX
Suffix for backup files.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test
Test archive integrity.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLON_WRAP
When unset (default), use the built-in rewrite implementation.
When set to
.BR 1 ,
exec the stem of
.B $0
from
.B PATH
(\fBcolon-zip\fR → \fBzip\fR).
When set to a program name, exec that program instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zip (1),
.BR colon-unzip (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
